m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: L-Alanine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: This synthesis network for L-alanine is constructed strictly around atom and charge conservation and explicit balancing. Each reaction includes all required byproducts, with well-defined formulas and intermediates. Multiple convergent prebiotic routes are supplied, incorporating Strecker, reductive amination, aldehyde hydrocarbonylation, nitrile hydrolysis, transamination, and aminonitrile pathways. Environments span hydrothermal vent, surface, and biochemical settings. All molecular nodes are explicitly defined and only referenced AFTER introduction. Each path is connected, balanced, and justified by experimental or conceptual precedent where possible. Ten pathways are presented, ensuring a robust and neutral exploration of L-alanine prebiotic synthesis.\n\nMOLECULES (17 nodes):\n  - mol_001: CO2 (carbon dioxide) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CH4 (methane) [starting]\n  - mol_003: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_004: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_005: H2O (water) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_006: CH2O (formaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C2H4O (acetaldehyde) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C2H3NO (acetonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H4O3 (pyruvic acid) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C3H5NO (2-aminopropanal) [intermediate]\n  - mol_011: C3H5NO (alanine nitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: C3H5NO2 (L-alanine) [target]\n  - mol_013: C3H5NO2 (DL-alanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: C3H5NO2 (2-cyanopropanoic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: H2 (hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_016: C2H5NH2 (ethylamine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C3H7NO (2-amino-1-propanol) [intermediate]\n\nREACTIONS (17 nodes):\n  - rxn_001: mol_001, mol_015 -> mol_002, mol_005 (Sabatier-type CO2 reduction to methane) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_002: mol_002, mol_001 -> mol_006, mol_005 (Methane partial oxidation to formaldehyde) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_003: mol_002, mol_003 -> mol_004, mol_005 (HCN formation from methane/ammonia/shock) [Surface]\n  - rxn_004: mol_006 -> mol_007 (Formaldehyde dimerization to acetaldehyde) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_005: mol_007, mol_003, mol_004, mol_005 -> mol_011 (Strecker amino acid synthesis (alanine)) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_011, mol_005 -> mol_013, mol_003 (Alanine nitrile hydrolysis to DL-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_007: mol_009, mol_003, mol_015 -> mol_013, mol_005 (Pyruvate amination to alanine (reductive amination)) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_008: mol_007, mol_001, mol_005 -> mol_009 (Acetaldehyde carboxylation to pyruvate) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_009: mol_013 -> mol_012 (Alanine racemization (DL to L-alanine)) [Biochemical]\n  - rxn_010: mol_008, mol_005 -> mol_016, mol_004 (Acetonitrile hydrolysis to ethylamine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_016, mol_001, mol_005 -> mol_013, mol_002 (Ethylamine carboxylation to alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_012: mol_006, mol_004 -> mol_014 (Formaldehyde plus HCN to 2-hydroxypropanenitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_013: mol_014, mol_003, mol_005 -> mol_013, mol_004 (2-cyanopropanoic acid hydrolysis to DL-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_010, mol_005 -> mol_013 (2-aminopropanal hydrolysis to DL-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_015: mol_006, mol_016 -> mol_017, mol_005 (Formaldehyde plus methylamine to 2-amino-1-propanol) [Surface]\n  - rxn_016: mol_017 -> mol_013, mol_005 (2-amino-1-propanol oxidation to DL-alanine) [Surface]\n  - rxn_017: mol_006, mol_003 -> mol_010, mol_005 (Formaldehyde plus ammonia to aminopropanal) [Surface]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Classic Strecker Amino Acid Synthesis (4 steps)\n  - P2: Reductive Amination of Pyruvate (4 steps)\n  - P3: Acetonitrile Hydrolysis and Amine Carboxylation (4 steps)\n  - P4: Hydroxypropanenitrile Pathway (3 steps)\n  - P5: Aminopropanal Hydrolysis Route (3 steps)\n  - P6: Amino Alcohol Oxidation Pathway (4 steps)\n  - P7: HCN-Based Early Strecker Variant (4 steps)\n  - P8: Pyruvate From Hydrothermal Carboxylation (4 steps)\n  - P9: Formaldehyde/Methylamine Condensation (4 steps)\n  - P10: Aminopropanal From Methane/Methanol (4 steps)\n\n\n=== DETERMINISTIC ATOM/CHARGE BALANCE CHECK (RDKit) ===\nComputed programmatically from each molecule's InChI (via RDKit) or stated formula. Reactions list no coefficients, so a reaction counts as balanced if some positive integer coefficients (<= 24) conserve every element and net charge.\nSummary: 17 reactions | 2 balanced as written | 2 balanceable with coefficients | 13 UNBALANCED | 0 unchecked\n  - rxn_001 balanceable: CO2 + 4 H2 -> CH4 + 2 H2O\n  - rxn_002 UNBALANCED: CH4 + CO2 -> CH2O + H2O | reactants minus products: C+1 | balanceable if adding: H2O as reactant; H2 as reactant; CO as product; O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_003 UNBALANCED: CH4 + NH3 -> HCN + H2O | reactants minus products: H+4, O-1 | balanceable if adding: CO2 as reactant; O2 as reactant\n  - rxn_004 UNBALANCED: CH2O -> C2H4O | reactants minus products: C-1, H-2 | balanceable if adding: O2 as product\n  - rxn_005 UNBALANCED: C2H4O + NH3 + HCN + H2O -> C3H5NO | reactants minus products: H+4, O+2 | balanceable if adding: H2O as product; CO2 as product; O2 as product\n  - rxn_006 balanceable: C3H5NO + 2 H2O -> C3H5NO2 + NH3\n  - rxn_008 UNBALANCED: C2H4O + CO2 + H2O -> C3H4O3 | reactants minus products: H+2, O+1 | bala